SUMMARY:PVPMC Workshop 2027: Abstracts due (23:59 UTC+12 (assumed))
DESCRIPTION:PV Performance Modeling Collaborative Workshop (PVPMC Workshop 
 2027)\n\nAbstracts due: 18 Dec 2026\, 23:59 UTC+12 (assumed)\n\nConference
 : May 11-13\, 2027\nLocation: Sacramento\, USA\n\nThe call for papers stat
 es no timezone. This is counted as UTC+12\, the earliest it could plausibl
 y mean\, so the countdown runs out before the real deadline rather than af
 ter it.\n\nCo-organized by Sandia National Laboratories\, GroundWork Renew
 ables and Terabase Energy. Abstracts are at most 300 words plus one figure
 \, with a short summary for the program\, submitted at https://abstracts.p
 vpmc-workshops.org/. All presentations must be technically focused\; sales
  pitches are not accepted. Proposals for software tutorials and PV technic
 al working group meetings are also invited. Students who submit an abstrac
 t and a one-page research statement may be eligible for free registration 
 and a travel grant.\n\nCall for papers: https://pvpmc.sandia.gov/\nDetails
 : https://powersystemdeadlines.org/conference/pvpmc27
LOCATION:Sacramento\, USA
URL;VALUE=URI:https://pvpmc.sandia.gov/
CATEGORIES:Renewables,Energy Storage
